# release-roadmap priority-queue restructure MINOR

2026-05-13. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood publish per
ASK-FIRST.

Lands the §4 restructure of `docs/release-roadmap.md` — from a
pre-numbered chain of forward-looking releases to a priority-ordered
queue of scope-descriptive, unnumbered candidates. Each candidate
carries: stable slug, single-sentence objective, class tag
(PATCH/MINOR/MAJOR), AC family, constraints, source items, AI-time
estimate, and dependencies (keyed on candidate slugs for forward
deps; on shipped version-numbers when the dep is on already-shipped
work).

The number-derivation recipe is documented in
`docs/release-versioning-policy.md` as a new "Number derivation at
build-commence time" section: `next_number = bump(current_version,
candidate_class)`. The recipe binds at build-commence-time, not at
queue-authoring-time; priority can change by reordering and class
can change by re-tagging, both without renumbering.

Reclassification audit deliverable lives as a §4-prelude inside
`docs/release-roadmap.md`. The audit is rescoped at build-time
(2026-05-13): the historical section walks already-shipped versions
read-only (surface mis-classifications; no retroactive renames per
HARD HALT — would break published tags); the forward-looking
section walks remaining unshipped §4 entries and re-tags class per
`docs/release-versioning-policy.md` definitions.

`docs/release-roadmap-dependency-map.md` is re-keyed from
version-numbers to candidate slugs in its dependency rows. SOFT
update — dep-graph itself unchanged; only row labels.

Composes with `feedback_version_numbers_at_release_time` (the
